   :criterion-text
   "Library consumer criteria interface/behavior/a3/prompt-authority-rendering: Invoke the actual STD13 public API against declared Domain/Runtime providers under this retained semantic contract: A3: emit typed prompt schemas, tool visibility, authority/taint maps, render hashes and compatibility policy. Validate format/schema, canonicalization, per-field taint and intended use before typed output admission. Reject arbitrary model-selected schemas, illegal partial outputs, undeclared tools and breaking output changes mislabeled compatible. Refusals follow a typed branch; repair policy and attempts are recorded. Secret-to-provider flow requires explicit policy; no-store responses retain only permitted hashes and facts. The inherited prompt-authority bridge retains approved sanitizer OR approved delimiter policy without promoting data to instruction authority or clearing source/taint, grant, secret or review obligations. SAFE13 acceptance: inspect model/provider/version, input/output schemas, nondeterminism, real external cost, retention, safety and replay records. Preserve structured prompt roles and provenance; reject untrusted grant/policy changes, privileged concatenation without approved sanitization/delimiting, and unvalidated tool arguments. Distinguish read-only/write/destructive/external/privileged tools; explicit grants and required human/policy decisions bind action/diff, reviewer, time and result before invocation. Generated code carries model/prompt origins and passes ordinary compiler/package checks before execution. Memory remains tainted absent trust metadata and enforces retention/redaction/privacy/deletion and secret policy. Check exact/audit replay and idempotent side effects through Runtime; prompt comments are not review decisions. The semantic producer retains its compilation, policy and provider responsibilities. This library leaf must expose the same accepted/refused predicate through its own callable boundary, retaining actual call/results, typed failures, schema/effect/grant/replay/origin identities as applicable. Reject a bypassed or weakened check, a mismatched provider result, or an export/manifest name used instead of actual API invocation. This is consumer acceptance, not new evidence that the underlying service or API is implemented.",
