   :criterion-text
   "Library consumer criteria interface/behavior/a1/human-review-gate, interface/behavior/a1/tool-authority: Invoke the actual STD13 public API against declared Domain/Runtime providers under this retained semantic contract: Source acceptance for A1-A11 remains open. A1: lower all declared AI forms through syntax, typed core and legal profiles into linked manifests, preserving source/macro origins, every AI effect, explicit replay modes and runtime audit records. Reject ambient credentials, hidden adapter effects, missing model or schema identities, generated source bypassing the normal compiler pipeline, and privileged deployments without review policy or required evaluation evidence. A4-A5: emit tool and agent manifests with complete dependencies and separate memory read/write modes. Tool declaration, agent toolset, package/deployment grant, scoped runtime handle and policy must all agree. Plans and model text grant no authority. Validate tool and agent results, expose implementation effects, normalize foreign errors, redact logs and model-facing descriptions, and record agent identity on every invocation event. Privileged tools require review policy; non-idempotent retries/replay require declared idempotency or compensation. Generated agent source re-enters compiler validation. A10: compile typed review declarations with action, actor/role, displayed evidence and evidence hash, payload hash, timestamp, expiry, revocation, denial/timeout, replay and emergency rules. Block required actions until matching valid review; reject absent records, wrong roles, changed payloads, expiry or revocation. Display enough typed evidence for the decision, follow denial as a workflow outcome, and reuse recorded decisions only under the declared replay policy. Audit requests and lifecycle transitions with redaction and permitted hashes. The semantic producer retains its compilation, policy and provider responsibilities. This library leaf must expose the same accepted/refused predicate through its own callable boundary, retaining actual call/results, typed failures, schema/effect/grant/replay/origin identities as applicable. Reject a bypassed or weakened check, a mismatched provider result, or an export/manifest name used instead of actual API invocation. This is consumer acceptance, not new evidence that the underlying service or API is implemented.",
